{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CfZtrbvkxPYNJokNpFVj6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Repository findings:**\n- Order entity: `Order.kt:11` — no status field currently\n- OrderController: `OrderController.kt:22` (create), `OrderController.kt:37` (getById) \n- OrderRepository: `OrderRepository.kt:15` (save), findById, existsById\n- ShipmentStatus enum: `Shipment.kt:23` — CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED\n- ShipmentRepository: `ShipmentRepository.kt` — no findByOrderId method\n- ShipmentController: `ShipmentController.kt:26` (create) — no order validation\n- Exception handling: `ApiExceptions.kt:19` (ResourceNotFoundException), `ApiExceptions.kt:23` (ConflictException)\n- ErrorCode enum: `ApiError.kt:31-36` — ORDER_NOT_FOUND, ORDER_ALREADY_EXISTS, SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS, VALIDATION_FAILED\n- GlobalExceptionHandler: `GlobalExceptionHandler.kt:16` centralizes exception → response conversion\n\n**Conventions this codebase has:**\n1. Status tracking via enums (ShipmentStatus already exists)\n2. In-memory repositories with ConcurrentHashMap backing\n3. Controllers throw ApiExceptions; GlobalExceptionHandler converts to ApiError envelopes\n4. All failure responses include error code, message, and optional fields\n5. Tests assert both status and jsonPath on response body\n6. Repositories have clear, findById, existsById, findAll, save patterns\n\n**Affected files:**\n1. `Order.kt` — add status field and OrderStatus enum\n2. `OrderController.kt` — add POST /{orderId}/cancel endpoint\n3. `ShipmentRepository.kt` — add findByOrderId method to support cascade cancel\n4. `ShipmentController.kt` — add validation to reject shipment creation for CANCELLED orders\n5. `ApiError.kt` — add error code for shipment creation on cancelled order\n6. `OrderControllerTest.kt` — add tests for cancel scenarios\n7. `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` — add test for shipment creation on cancelled order\n\n**Risks:**\n- All-or-nothing semantics: if any shipment is CONFIRMED, the entire cancel must fail atomically\n- Idempotency: cancelling already CANCELLED order must not fail\n- Cascade updates: all CREATED shipments must be updated in same transaction/call\n- Existing tests: existing OrderControllerTest and ShipmentControllerTest must continue to pass\n\n**Open questions:**\n- None identified that would change correct behaviour. The ticket clearly specifies all cases: idempotency, conflict prevention, cascade behavior, and error codes.\n\nNow I'll move to DESIGN.\n\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n\n**Proposed change, file by file:**\n\n1. **Order.kt**: Add `OrderStatus` enum (ACTIVE, CANCELLED) and `status: OrderStatus` field to Order data class. New orders are ACTIVE by default.\n\n2. **OrderController.kt**: Add `cancelOrder` method mapped to `POST /{orderId}/cancel`. Logic:\n   - Find the order by orderId; if not found, throw ResourceNotFoundException (404)\n   - Check all shipments for this order: if ANY is CONFIRMED, throw ConflictException (409) without changing anything\n   - Update the order status to CANCELLED\n   - Update all CREATED shipments for this order to CANCELLED\n   - Return the updated order with 200 OK\n   - If the order is already CANCELLED, this succeeds without error (idempotent)\n\n3. **ShipmentRepository.kt**: Add `findByOrderId(orderId: String): List<Shipment>` method to find all shipments for an order.\n\n4. **ShipmentController.kt**: In the create method, after checking if the shipment already exists, verify the order is not CANCELLED. If it is, throw ConflictException with appropriate error code.\n\n5. **ApiError.kt**: Add error code `ORDER_CANCELLED` to the ErrorCode enum.\n\n6. **OrderControllerTest.kt**: Add tests for:\n   - Cancelling an ACTIVE order returns 200 and the order is CANCELLED\n   - Cancelling an ACTIVE order cancels all CREATED shipments\n   - Cancelling already CANCELLED order succeeds (idempotent)\n   - Cancelling when a shipment is CONFIRMED returns 409 and nothing changes\n   - Cancelling unknown order returns 404\n\n7. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt**: Add test for:\n   - Creating shipment for CANCELLED order returns 409 with ORDER_CANCELLED error code\n\n**Alternative considered and rejected:**\n\n*Alternative: Create a separate OrderService layer for cancel logic*\n- Rejected because: The codebase doesn't use service layer, controllers directly use repositories. Adding a service would diverge from existing patterns without justifying the added complexity. The cancel logic is straightforward enough to live in the controller.\n\n*Alternative: Use database transactions for atomicity*\n- Rejected because: The repository is in-memory ConcurrentHashMap-based. The existing codebase does not use Spring Data or transactions. Single-threaded request handling in Spring MVC provides sufficient atomicity for this fixture.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n1. **Happy path - Cancel ACTIVE order with CREATED shipments:**\n   - Read: Order by ID → OrderRepository.findById\n   - Read: All shipments for order → ShipmentRepository.findByOrderId\n   - Validate: No shipment is CONFIRMED\n   - Write: Order status = CANCELLED → OrderRepository.save\n   - Write: Shipment status = CANCELLED (for each CREATED shipment) → ShipmentRepository.save (loop)\n   - Return: Updated Order, HTTP 200\n\n2. **Idempotent cancel (order already CANCELLED):**\n   - Read: Order by ID → OrderRepository.findById\n   - Validate: No shipment is CONFIRMED (all are either CREATED or CANCELLED)\n   - Write: Order status = CANCELLED (no-op, already CANCELLED)\n   - Return: Order, HTTP 200\n\n3. **Conflict - CONFIRMED shipment exists:**\n   - Read: Order by ID → OrderRepository.findById\n   - Read: All shipments for order → ShipmentRepository.findByOrderId\n   - Validate: Find CONFIRMED shipment\n   - Throw: ConflictException(SHIPMENT_CONFIRMED_CANNOT_CANCEL, \"Cannot cancel order...\")\n   - Return: Error envelope, HTTP 409\n   - Side effects: NONE (all-or-nothing)\n\n4. **Not found - unknown order:**\n   - Read: Order by ID → OrderRepository.findById\n   - Validate: Not found\n   - Throw: ResourceNotFoundException(ORDER_NOT_FOUND, \"No order with id...\")\n   - Return: Error envelope, HTTP 404\n\n5. **Shipment creation on CANCELLED order:**\n   - Read: Order by ID → OrderRepository.findById\n   - Validate: Order exists AND is CANCELLED\n   - Throw: ConflictException(ORDER_CANCELLED, \"Cannot create shipment for cancelled order\")\n   - Return: Error envelope, HTTP 409\n   - Side effects: NONE (shipment not created)\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n1. `cancelActivOrder_returnsCancelledOrder` — POST /orders/O-1/cancel after creating O-1, verify status is CANCELLED, HTTP 200\n2. `cancelActivOrder_cancelsCREATEDShipments` — Create O-1 with shipments S-1 (CREATED), S-2 (CREATED), cancel O-1, verify both shipments are CANCELLED\n3. `cancelAlreadyCancelledOrder_succeeds` — Cancel O-1 twice, second call succeeds without error, HTTP 200\n4. `cancelOrder_conflictIfCONFIRMEDShipmentExists` — Create O-1 with S-1 in CONFIRMED status, cancel O-1, expect HTTP 409, verify O-1 is still ACTIVE, S-1 is still CONFIRMED\n5. `cancelUnknownOrder_returns404` — Cancel non-existent order, expect HTTP 404 with ORDER_NOT_FOUND code\n6. `createShipment_conflictIfOrderIsCancelled` — Cancel O-1, then create shipment for O-1, expect HTTP 409 with ORDER_CANCELLED code\n\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n\nLet me start implementing the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2029,"cache_read_input_tokens":20594,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2029},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"72146fd7-f6ff-4755-b7b9-bfa1468612e1","uuid":"5dff6a14-8de0-4c71-9c5