{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CfZtzT8Q5pevsW8oF2izy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! All 21 tests passed (4 existing order tests + 6 new cancel tests + 5 existing shipment tests + 2 new cancelled order tests + 3 customer tests + 1 application test). The build was successful with no failures.\n\n<<PHASE:REVIEW>>\n\n**Acceptance criteria mapping:**\n\n1. ✅ **Existing build passes.** — BUILD SUCCESS, all tests pass (21/21)\n\n2. ✅ **Existing tests pass.** — All 4 existing OrderControllerTest tests pass, all 5 existing ShipmentControllerTest tests pass, CustomerControllerTest passes\n\n3. ✅ **`POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel` cancels an active order, persists it, and cancels that order's `CREATED` shipments.**\n   - Implemented in `OrderController.kt:46-76` (cancel method)\n   - Tested by `cancelActivOrder_returnsCancelledOrder` and `cancelActivOrder_cancelsCREATEDShipments`\n   - Order status persisted via `OrderRepository.save(cancelledOrder)`\n   - Shipments persisted via loop calling `ShipmentRepository.save(shipment.copy(status = ShipmentStatus.CANCELLED))`\n\n4. ✅ **Error responses are consistent with the rest of this API.**\n   - ResourceNotFoundException (404) for unknown order — consistent with existing error handling\n   - ConflictException (409) for CONFIRMED shipment — consistent with ORDER_ALREADY_EXISTS pattern\n   - ConflictException (409) for cancelled order shipment creation — consistent with pattern\n   - All use the ApiError envelope with code, message, fields\n\n5. ✅ **A repeated cancel succeeds; a cancel blocked by a `CONFIRMED` shipment changes nothing; an unknown order is refused; a shipment for a cancelled order is refused.**\n   - Idempotent cancel: `cancelAlreadyCancelledOrder_succeeds` — cancels twice, both succeed\n   - CONFIRMED shipment conflict: `cancel_order_returns_409_if_any_shipment_is_CONFIRMED_and_changes_nothing` — verifies no state changes\n   - Unknown order: `cancelUnknownOrder_returns404` — returns 404 with ORDER_NOT_FOUND\n   - Cancelled order shipment: `rejects_shipment_creation_for_cancelled_order_with_409` — returns 409 with ORDER_CANCELLED\n\n6. ✅ **No new Maven dependency appears.** — pom.xml unchanged, only added use of existing dependencies\n\n7. ✅ **No unrelated production file changes.** — Only modified:\n   - `Order.kt` — added status field and OrderStatus enum (required)\n   - `OrderController.kt` — added cancel method and shipment repository injection (required)\n   - `ShipmentRepository.kt` — added findByOrderId method (required for cascade cancel)\n   - `ShipmentController.kt` — added order repository injection and cancelled order validation (required)\n   - `ApiError.kt` — added error codes (required)\n   - Test files only (OrderControllerTest.kt, ShipmentControllerTest.kt)\n\n**Diff review:**\n\n1. **Order.kt** — Added `OrderStatus` enum and `status` field with default `ACTIVE`. This is necessary for order lifecycle tracking as specified in the ticket. The default parameter ensures backward compatibility with existing order creation calls.\n\n2. **OrderController.kt** — Added `cancel` method (POST /{orderId}/cancel) with complete business logic:\n   - Finds order or throws 404\n   - Checks for CONFIRMED shipments and throws 409 if found (all-or-nothing)\n   - Updates order to CANCELLED\n   - Cancels all CREATED shipments\n   - Returns updated order with 200 OK\n   - Idempotent because cancelling an already CANCELLED order succeeds\n\n3. **ShipmentRepository.kt** — Added `findByOrderId` method to support cancel operation's need to find all shipments for an order.\n\n4. **ShipmentController.kt** — Added validation in `create` method to reject shipment creation for CANCELLED orders, while preserving existing behavior for non-existent orders.\n\n5. **ApiError.kt** — Added two new error codes:\n   - `ORDER_CANCELLED` — for shipment creation on cancelled order\n   - `SHIPMENT_CONFIRMED_CANNOT_CANCEL` — for cancel attempt with CONFIRMED shipment\n\n6. **OrderControllerTest.kt** — Added 6 new tests covering all cancel scenarios:\n   - Status field initialization (ACTIVE)\n   - Happy path cancel\n   - Cascade cancel of CREATED shipments\n   - Idempotent cancel\n   - Conflict with CONFIRMED shipment (all-or-nothing)\n   - Unknown order 404\n\n7. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Added 2 new tests:\n   - Reject shipment creation for cancelled order\n   - Allow shipment creation for non-existent order (preserves current behavior)\n\n**Unresolved findings:**\n\nNone. All requirements are implemented and tested.\n\n<<PHASE:DONE>>\n\n```\nRequirement   Customers can cancel active orders until a carrier accepts a shipment, with order status tracking and all-or-nothing semantics.\nChanged       Order.kt — Added OrderStatus enum (ACTIVE, CANCELLED) and status field to Order\n              OrderController.kt — Added POST /{orderId}/cancel endpoint with complete business logic\n              ShipmentRepository.kt — Added findByOrderId method to support cascade cancel\n              ShipmentController.kt — Added validation to reject shipment creation for CANCELLED orders\n              ApiError.kt — Added ORDER_CANCELLED and SHIPMENT_CONFIRMED_CANNOT_CANCEL error codes\n              OrderControllerTest.kt — Added 6 tests for cancel operation and status handling\n              ShipmentControllerTest.kt — Added 2 tests for cancelled order shipment rejection and non-existent order behavior\nTests         cancelActivOrder_returnsCancelledOrder — POST /cancel returns 200 with CANCELLED status\n              cancelActivOrder_cancelsCREATEDShipments — POST /cancel updates all CREATED shipments to CANCELLED\n              cancelAlreadyCancelledOrder_succeeds — Cancelling CANCELLED order succeeds (idempotent)\n              cancel_order_returns_409_if_any_shipment_is_CONFIRMED_and_changes_nothing — 409 conflict, no state changes\n              cancelUnknownOrder_returns404 — Unknown order returns 404 with ORDER_NOT_FOUND\n              rejects_shipment_creation_for_cancelled_order_with_409 — Shipment creation on CANCELLED order returns 409 with ORDER_CANCELLED\n              allows_shipment_creation_for_non_existent_order — Non-existent order does not block shipment creation (current behavior preserved)\n              newly_created_order_has_ACTIVE_status — New orders have ACTIVE status by default\nVerification  Command: ./mvnw test\n              Result: BUILD SUCCESS, 21 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors\n              All existing tests continue to pass; 8 new tests verify cancel functionality\nNot done      None — all acceptance criteria satisfied, all tests passing, no forbidden files changed\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3331,"cache_read_input_tokens":35730,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3331},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"72146fd7-f6ff-4755-b7b9-bfa1468612e1","uuid":"32f25478-ef93-4e7e-8673-91625ff77225","timestamp":"2026-09-30T15:56:32.728Z","request_id":"req_011CfZtzSkpudpoMcFABoAcq"}
